{"name":"Blossom Tint","hex":"#fbd6ca","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blossom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flower, especially one indicating that a fruit tree is fruiting;  a mass of such flowers.","The state or season of producing such flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have, or open into, blossoms; to bloom.","To begin to thrive or flourish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blossom"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in spring."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png/330px-Badamwari_Flower_Series_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blossom","wikidata":"Q2047589"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped